          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: The witness, driving at high speed (130 km/h) in their vehicle, observes a bright white halo spinning in the sky. The information provided in the questionnaire (no gendarmerie procedural report) does not specify the exact location or duration of the observation. However, the vehicle was traveling north-south, and the driver was observing south through their windshield. At the time of the observation, SIRIUS, the brightest star in our sky, was in the direction of observation. The variable, sparkling nature, combined with the visual fatigue of driving, could explain the spinning impression of the observation. A precise verification is not possible, but the probable observation of the star Sirius could explain the observation.",
